# lens-dissolved-modules.allow — hits that are correct as written.
#
# Format: <path-relative-to-spec-dir><TAB><substring>. Both must match, so a new stale reference in
# an already-listed file still fires. Every entry needs a reason above it: this
# file is where the judgment is recorded, not where it is hidden.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-18 in the spexmachina-kfem drift triage.

# The journal is append-only and answers for nodes that no longer exist, so a
# removal record names the module the removed node lived in — permanently. A
# leaf documenting that format has to quote such a record; rewriting these
# examples to name a live module would make them describe events that cannot
# occur. Verified against spec/.history.jsonl, which holds exactly this shape.
map/arch_mapping_store.md	"module": "impact"
map/arch_mapping_store.md	"path": "impact/arch_action_classifier.md"
map/arch_map_command.md	"module":"impact"
schema/test_bead_map_schema.md	"module":"impact"
schema/test_bead_map_schema.md	the change-event fixture with `"path": "impact/

# A close op's reason carries the module the removed node lived in, for the
# same reason. Sample output of a real changeset.
plan/arch_changeset_builder.md	"reason": "Spec node modified: apply/ApplyCommand"

# An explicitly historical sentence naming a pre-decouple Go path. The word
# "pre-decouple" is doing the work; the path is not a live location.
adapters/arch_br_reference_adapter.md	pre-decouple `apply/bead_creator.go
